      "id": 12370,
      "name": "DrScott",
      "username": "DrScott",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-21T13:35:45.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm playing a game currently with Expatiette and it's got me thinking, again, about her. &nbsp;Specifically her Incendiary Rounds. &nbsp;They change her damage to fire and add 1, and I'm trying to think why this is a particularly desirable. &nbsp;The damage buff is a duplicate trick to Hollow Points, which &nbsp;give a much better damage buff. &nbsp;One possibility is if a villain should be immune to projectile damage, which frankly doesn't happen often. &nbsp;And if it does, Cryo Rounds also changes the damage type and the damage debuff is both not duplicated by another ammo type and a quite useful status attack. &nbsp;The other might be if paired with Ra or having some other method of increasing specifically fire damage. &nbsp;Which I feel is even less likely to happen than the first case. &nbsp; Functionally, Incendiary Rounds just don't seem to have much point beyond the +1, and HPs do it better.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(As a potential alternate I'm considering house ruling them into \"Armor Piercing Rounds\" - the effect of which is to make the attack irreducible. &nbsp;It makes great sense thematically and expands Expat's bag of tricks while getting rid of a redundant ammo type.)</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:53.100Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
