      "raw": "<p>I&#39;m playing a game currently with Expatiette and it&#39;s got me thinking, again, about her. &nbsp;Specifically her Incendiary Rounds. &nbsp;They change her damage to fire and add 1, and I&#39;m trying to think why this is a particularly desirable. &nbsp;The damage buff is a duplicate trick to Hollow Points, which &nbsp;give a much better damage buff. &nbsp;One possibility is if a villain should be immune to projectile damage, which frankly doesn&#39;t happen often. &nbsp;And if it does, Cryo Rounds also changes the damage type and the damage debuff is both not duplicated by another ammo type and a quite useful status attack. &nbsp;The other might be if paired with Ra or having some other method of increasing specifically fire damage. &nbsp;Which I feel is even less likely to happen than the first case. &nbsp; Functionally, Incendiary Rounds just don&#39;t seem to have much point beyond the +1, and HPs do it better.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(As a potential alternate I&#39;m considering house ruling them into &quot;Armor Piercing Rounds&quot; - the effect of which is to make the attack irreducible. &nbsp;It makes great sense thematically and expands Expat&#39;s bag of tricks while getting rid of a redundant ammo type.)</p>",
